Fixed and committed as 5824b133 (Fixes #1130). Build, clippy with -D warnings, fmt check and the full test suite all pass: 7204 tests across 34 suites, 0 failures.

The bug, checked against the old binary first. The shell yoyo review path joined all arguments into one string, then split it on spaces again, so a word after -- was read as a flag:
• review -- --quick set the quick effort and reviewed the working tree.
• review -- --pr5 asked gh for PR 5 instead of looking for a file.
• review -- "a  b.rs" was squeezed to a b.rs.

The fix. verb_flags::review_args now reads effort and target straight from the argument list into a ReviewArgs struct:
• --quick and --thorough only count before --.
• The target is never split on spaces again, so one quoted argument stays one path.
• A target that came only from after -- goes to a new function, build_review_content_operand (the commit-range/file part of build_review_content, moved out). It is never read as --pr, but -- HEAD~3..HEAD still works as a range.

The REPL /review doesn't use this path and behaves as before.

Tests. There's one row per input the old join-and-split handled the same way:
• -- --quick, -- --thorough and -- --pr5 now each report file not found for that word.
• A path with spaces stays one path, with or without --.
• --quick, --quick src/x.rs, a bare review and the --pr N forms behave as before.
• "" and -- "" still review staged/unstaged changes; I checked that's what they did before.
• --quik still gets #1129's exit-2 "did you mean --quick" refusal.

The new cases run against the real binary and compare the error line with colour codes removed.

For the positive control I put the old re-split back on the shell path (marked NEUTERED). The -- --quick row then failed with the old "not in a git repository". I restored it in the same command; the tree is back to green with no markers left.

Things to know:
• One of my own expected values was wrong at first: a bare -- does mark the target as coming after --, though the result is still the staged review. I fixed that table row; the code was right.
• Spaces at the start or end of a target are still trimmed, as before. A quoted path keeps the spaces inside it but loses edge spaces.
• docs/src/usage/commands.md now says that -- ends flags. The remaining #1130 mentions in the code are history notes, so nothing needs retargeting once the issue closes.

